mathematical_statement.body_tex:
\label{cook-nagel}
Consider the ideal $I=(x^{a_1+t}, y^{a_2+t}, z^{a_3+t}, x^{a_1}y^{a_2}z^{a_3})\subseteq\F[x, y, z]$ where $a_1, a_2, a_3, t$ satisfy the following three conditions:
\begin{equation}\label{conditions}
    0<a_1\le a_2 \le a_3\le 2(a_1+a_2),\ 3\ \text{divides}\ a_1+a_2+a_3, \ \text{and} \ t\ge \frac{a_1+a_2+a_3}{3}.
\end{equation}
If $(a_1, a_2, a_3, t)$ is not $(2, 9, 13, 9)$ or $(3, 7, 14, 9)$, then $\F[x, y, z]/I$ fails WLP if and only if $t$ is even, $a_1+a_2+a_3$ is odd, and $a_1=a_2$ or $a_2=a_3$.

