mathematical_statement.body_tex:
\label{generalized_bound_conjecture}
        Let $K\subset\mathbb{R}^2$ be a symmetric convex body with strictly convex $C^1$ boundary. If $A,B\subset\mathbb{R}^2$ are nonempty compact sets, then
        \begin{equation}\label{eq:conjecture_symmetric_K}
            d^{(K)}(A+B)\leq 2 \max\left\{d^{(K)}(\textup{vert}(T)):T\in\mathcal{R}_K(d^{(K)}(A),d^{(K)}(B))\right\}.
        \end{equation}
        Moreover, for any nonnegative real numbers $\alpha$ and $\beta$, there exist nonempty compact sets $A,B\subset\mathbb{R}^2$ such that $d^{(K)}(A)=\alpha$, $d^{(K)}(B)=\beta$, and \eqref{eq:conjecture_symmetric_K} is equality.

