\label{conj:lattice}
If $\lambda$ is a triangular partition such that its top-down tableau $\theta$ is a sim-sym tableau, there exists a Schur-positive symmetric function $\lambda$ such that 
\begin{equation}
A_\lambda(q,t,1) = \sum_{\tau \preceq \mu} q^{\dist(\tau, \mu)} t^{\ssim_\theta(\tau, \mu)}
\end{equation}
where the sum runs over intervals in the $\nu$-Tamari lattice of $\lambda$.

